      "core": "祈使句規範之核心本質：省略主詞 You，以原形動詞開頭；否定句用 Don't + 原形動詞。",
      "explanation": "本知識點著眼於「祈使句規範」之本質定義。依據 108 課綱核心素養，省略主詞 You，以原形動詞開頭；否定句用 Don't + 原形動詞。對應本課核心觀念：Adverbs of frequency (always, usually, often, sometimes, never) show how often an action happens. They come before action verbs but after be-verbs. The modal verb \"can\" expresses ability or permission and is followed by a base verb. \"There is\" and \"There are\" state existence.。在實際解題與概念理解時，必須牢記其成立之關鍵準則：實戰檢核與適用條件：Open the door, please. / Don't be late for school again.。避免僅死背名詞，而應從日常經驗（如：She is always on time. / He often plays baseball after school. / Can you swim? Yes, I can. / There is a cat on the roof, and there are three dogs in the yard.）理解其物理、數學或邏輯必然性。",
      "formula": "【實戰法則】省略主詞 You，以原形動詞開頭；否定句用 Don't + 原形動詞 ➔ 檢驗條件：Open the door, please. / Don't be late for school again.",
      "practicalTip": "大考辨識關鍵：當題幹出現「頻率副詞、情態助動詞 can 與存在句、第一句為 Lily is usually early.，be 動詞 is 在 usually 前；若換一般動詞，可說 Lily usually arrives early.。、祈使句規範、感嘆句結構、附加問句前肯後否」等關鍵條件或圖表特徵時立即啟動本課模型。。考場避坑：【高頻盲點】Do not put frequency adverbs before be-verbs (say \"He is always kind\", not \"He always is kind\"). In There is/are sentences, verb agreement depends on the noun that immediately follows.",
